WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.054
Let's install HarnessStation on Linux.

2
00:00:02.054 --> 00:00:06.000
Two ways to do it, and one common launch failure that has a one-line fix.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:06.948
You've got two options.

4
00:00:06.948 --> 00:00:10.206
The AppImage is a single portable file that runs anywhere — nothing to install.

5
00:00:10.206 --> 00:00:12.928
Or, on Debian and Ubuntu, install the dot-deb package system-wide.

6
00:00:12.928 --> 00:00:14.000
Pick whichever you prefer.

7
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.100
For the AppImage, mark it executable with chmod plus x, then run it.

8
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:23.000
That's it — the app launches straight from the file.

9
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.352
Prefer a proper install?

10
00:00:24.352 --> 00:00:31.000
On Debian or Ubuntu, install the dot-deb with dpkg, and it'll show up in your application menu like any other program.

11
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:31.729
Now the gotcha.

12
00:00:31.729 --> 00:00:36.153
On a fresh system the AppImage sometimes just… doesn't start — no window, no obvious error.

13
00:00:36.153 --> 00:00:38.292
Nearly always it's a missing WebKit library.

14
00:00:38.292 --> 00:00:41.549
Install these two packages with apt, run it again, and it comes up.

15
00:00:41.549 --> 00:00:45.000
This is the single most common Linux issue, so keep this command handy.

16
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:45.706
One optional extra.

17
00:00:45.706 --> 00:00:49.645
If you want the app to speak using your system's built-in voices, install espeak-ng and speech-dispatcher.

18
00:00:49.645 --> 00:00:53.659
This is only for the system voice — the app's own neural voice, Kokoro, runs locally and needs none of this.

19
00:00:53.659 --> 00:00:56.000
So it's genuinely optional; skip it for now if you're not sure.

20
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Launch it, and you're running on Linux.

21
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.144
That covers installing on both platforms.

22
00:01:03.144 --> 00:01:07.330
Next, for anyone who wants to audit or avoid the unsigned binary, we build HarnessStation from source — and then we start our first real conversation.

23
00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.000
See you in the next one.

